= BITwiki Manifesto =

'''BITwiki is not a static encyclopedia. It is a living knowledge system built so useful intelligence can survive the moment, be examined, related, corrected, transcluded, and reused.'''

== Knowledge should compound ==

A meaningful contribution should not disappear merely because a conversation ended.

BIThub was developed around a recurring problem: useful research, reasoning, experiments, explanations, workflows, and corrections are easily lost inside disconnected chats, buried threads, private notes, and disposable AI outputs. The ecosystem exists to turn high-signal contribution into reusable intelligence.

A discussion may become an artifact. An artifact may become a reviewed reference. Stable knowledge may crystallize into BITwiki. A BITwiki page may expose new questions that return to BIThub for another cycle of research.

'''Useful intelligence should compound.'''

== Memory is more than storage ==

'''Storage saves data. Memory preserves useful context.'''

A pile of files is storage. Durable memory retains what the material means, why it matters, where it came from, how it relates to other knowledge, how it changed, and how it can be retrieved and reused.

BITwiki is therefore intended as structured memory: modular, referenceable, queryable, linked, versioned, and source-aware.

== Transposable, modular, composable ==

BITwiki is a Semantic MediaWiki-based knowledge system designed to be machine-queryable and human-legible at the same time.

Its long-running design constraints are:

* '''Transposability''' — useful knowledge can move across contexts and systems without losing its meaning.
* '''Modularity''' — meaningful components can be retrieved and reused independently.
* '''Composability''' — smaller knowledge units can assemble into larger structures.
* '''Depth and nuance''' — modularity must not flatten sophisticated subjects into shallow summaries.

The objective is not merely to make information shorter. The objective is to make knowledge easier to retrieve, examine, recombine, and deepen.

== Rational objectivity ==

'''Knowledge must be grounded in evidence, structured by logic, and free from undue influence. Speculative ideas are welcome but require clear labeling.'''

BITwiki does not claim to be perfectly unbiased and does not claim to know everything. Perspective is unavoidable; hidden perspective is more dangerous than explicit perspective.

Claims, interpretations, hypotheses, metaphors, worldview, and speculation should be distinguished when those differences matter. Evidence and provenance should remain inspectable.

== Multiple lenses, reality-bound ==

The project has deliberately explored scientific, engineering, philosophical, religious, esoteric, ecological, and mythopoetic lenses. These perspectives may provide useful conceptual tools, metaphors, historical knowledge, or alternative frames.

'''The bias is not an excuse for fantasy.''' Lenses are used to remain curious while staying pragmatic and reality-bound, not to escape evidence or convert metaphor into fact.

Diversity of thought is valuable when paired with intellectual honesty, explicit epistemic status, and the freedom to disagree.

== Systems thinking ==

BITwiki treats knowledge as relational. Topics influence and are influenced by larger systems. Articles should therefore support connections between concepts, implementations, evidence, history, domains, and applications rather than behaving as isolated text documents.

Systems science is a foundational orientation because a bit of information only becomes meaningful through distinctions, relations, transformations, and systems in which it participates.

== Progressive disclosure ==

BITwiki should serve different levels of expertise without forcing every reader or agent through the same amount of text.

A subject may expose a simple orientation, intermediate conceptual structure, advanced technical depth, and evidence/citations/historical development/controversy/implementation detail.

Transclusion and Book Matter allow a human or agent to pull exactly the portion required while preserving a deeper canonical object behind it.

== Knowledge as action ==

Knowledge should not terminate at description. Where appropriate, content should connect theory to application, tools, case studies, implementations, experiments, decision support, and practical consequences.

== Human agency ==

The human should emerge with:

* '''more clarity, not more dependence''';
* '''more dignity, not more compliance''';
* '''more self-respect, not more outsourcing of meaning''';
* '''more agency, not more coercion'''.

Constructs, agents, workflows, and automation should elevate human–AI symbiosis rather than obscure responsibility or replace human purpose.

== The knowledge continuum ==

BIThub is where the cognitive collective can think aloud, investigate, debate, test, and coordinate.

BITCORE is the cognitive and orchestration layer through which agents, Constructs, COREs, Nodes, Workspaces, tools, prompts, workflows, and human operators process work.

BITwiki is the durable semantic memory layer where accepted knowledge can be preserved in a modular, succinct, queryable, and reference-oriented form.

The objective is to '''maintain fidelity in the knowledge continuum''' as useful signal moves from live discourse into structured memory and back again.

== Prime directive ==

'''Do not consume passively. Generate Signal.'''

Observe. Contribute. Evolve.

Generate what is worth preserving. Preserve what is worth reusing. Revisit what can still be improved.

